"""
mining_pool_bridge.py — How this chain connects to the wider world.

THE CORE DISTINCTION:
  This is a PRIVATE application-specific blockchain.
  It mines locally using SHA-256 PoW — the same cryptographic principle as Bitcoin,
  but for a completely different purpose: encoding conviction levels for health claims.

  Bitcoin mining pools (Foundry USA, Braiins Pool, AntPool) mine for financial reward.
  This chain mines for EVIDENCE WEIGHT — no financial reward, no external miners.

  But they connect through specific protocols:

  CONNECTION 1 — Bitcoin via OpenTimestamps (free, open-source, proven):
    Take this chain's tip hash → submit to OpenTimestamps calendar server → it gets
    included in a Bitcoin transaction → that transaction enters the Bitcoin MEMPOOL →
    Foundry USA / Braiins Pool / AntPool / etc. mine it into the Bitcoin blockchain.
    Now this chain's existence is permanently timestamped at Bitcoin-level security.
    SHA-256 collision resistance + Bitcoin PoW (>$1B attack cost) = immutable proof.

  CONNECTION 2 — Ethereum (smart contracts):
    Deploy a Solidity contract that stores chain tip hashes and verifies claim blocks.
    Any third party can verify a claim against the contract without accessing raw PHI.
    Polygon L2 reduces gas to ~$0.001 per verification.

  CONNECTION 3 — DeSci protocols (VitaDAO, LabDAO, Bio Protocol, Molecule):
    Submit verified research findings to DeSci governance. These protocols are designed
    specifically for research data on blockchain. VitaDAO funds longevity research.
    LabDAO connects researchers to equipment. Bio Protocol provides DeSci infrastructure.

  CONNECTION 4 — Genomic data pools:
    ClinVar (clinical variants) · gnomAD (population frequencies) · UK Biobank
    (500k participants) · TCGA (cancer genome atlas) · All of Us (NIH diverse cohort).
    Read-only: this chain queries these pools to cross-verify its own claims.

  CONNECTION 5 — Brain/EEG data pools ("Brainspool"):
    "Brainspool" is not a single service — it is the concept of federated EEG/neural
    data networks that this system contributes to and reads from:
    · PhysioNet: 21,000+ clinical physiological records (waveform + annotation)
    · OpenNeuro: 1,000+ neuroimaging/EEG datasets (open access)
    · MOABB (Mother of All BCI Benchmarks): standardised EEG challenge datasets
    · OpenBCI community data: shared EEG recordings from OpenBCI users worldwide
    · BNCI Horizon: European BCI research data repository

    This chain's P300 responses, EEG epochs, and BCI interpretations could be
    (with consent) contributed to these pools to improve BCI classifiers for everyone.
    Equally, trained classifiers from these pools improve this chain's own BCI accuracy.

  ABOUT "MEMPOOL":
    The Bitcoin mempool is the waiting area for unconfirmed Bitcoin transactions.
    When OpenTimestamps submits this chain's hash to Bitcoin, it creates a Bitcoin
    transaction that enters the mempool. Mining pools (Foundry, Braiins, AntPool)
    then include that transaction in the next Bitcoin block they mine. From that point,
    the hash is permanently in the Bitcoin blockchain — immutable, publicly verifiable.

    The Bitcoin block number and transaction ID become this chain's external timestamp.

  ABOUT "BRAIINS POOL":
    Braiins Pool (originally Slush Pool, launched 2010 — the world's first Bitcoin
    mining pool) is a Bitcoin PoW pool using the open-source Stratum V2 protocol.
    It is NOT directly connected to this chain. But:
    · OpenTimestamps submissions are mined by whichever pool happens to mine the block
    · In 2026, Foundry USA (~30%), AntPool, Braiins, F2Pool etc. share Bitcoin hashrate
    · Whichever pool mines the Bitcoin block containing this chain's hash becomes the
      indirect custodian of that timestamp proof

RESEARCH GROUNDING:
  OpenTimestamps (Bitcoin developer Peter Todd):
    "Creates a proof of existence by committing a hash of your data into Bitcoin.
    Your file never leaves your machine; only its hash is used. Once anchored to Bitcoin,
    anyone can verify it using open tools — today or ten years from now."

  Standard-Compliant Blockchain Anchoring (Appl. Sci. 2025, 15(23), 12722):
    "Creates a Merkle tree of multiple document hashes and anchors only the root hash
    in a Bitcoin transaction. One company using this method is Intesi Group (Italy).
    The approach is fully compliant with RFC 3161."

  DeSci / Bio Protocol (Bitcoin Foundation Jun 2026):
    "BioDAOs — VitaDAO, AthenaDAO, ValleyDAO — self-fund research through decentralised
    governance. Bio Protocol provides infrastructure for multiple research communities."

  Blockchain in genomics (arXiv 2004.06795):
    "The global blockchain in genomic market grows at a CAGR of 66.42% during 2019-2029.
    Companies using blockchain in genomic data: Nebula Genomics, EncrypGen, Doc.AI."
"""

